<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:540f36ce85906f22e04358142a642eb1ee62246edececa49769191b82462a737> <https://example.org/slice/lineage> "A Field Guide to the Marrow Archipelago > the outer reefs"^^<https://example.org/slice/lineage> .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:540f36ce85906f22e04358142a642eb1ee62246edececa49769191b82462a737> <https://example.org/slice/ordinal> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:540f36ce85906f22e04358142a642eb1ee62246edececa49769191b82462a737> <https://example.org/slice/section> <https://example.org/slice/section:sha256:3ec00a24e3072978d4e8a1a97fcb6c281caff08b083c8893531c4475607872aa> .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:540f36ce85906f22e04358142a642eb1ee62246edececa49769191b82462a737> <https://example.org/slice/text> "3. Between the Anvil and the Comb the shelf drops away in three steps,\nand each step keeps its own crowd: the first holds the banded urchins\nthat the fishers call pinheads, the second the pale fans 🐚 that close\nat a shadow and open again a slow count later, and the third nothing at\nall that a diver has yet named, only a cold green water that the light\ngives up on well before the floor of it is reached by any lamp we own." .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:540f36ce85906f22e04358142a642eb1ee62246edececa49769191b82462a737> <https://example.org/slice/verse> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
